From: FP6 feature-push (misc agent)
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report charge_* in uAh on SM8350-family

On SM8350/SM8550-family pmic_glink firmware (FP6, qcom,milos-pmic-glink ->
QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550) battmgr->unit is never initialised because only the
SC8280XP info response sets it. It stays QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mWh (0), so the
advertised charge_full and charge_full_design return -ENODATA and there is no
charge_now/energy_now at all. UPower then reports energy 0 Wh and cannot
estimate time-to-empty/full.

Set the unit to mAh for the SM8350-family (the firmware reports these
properties in uAh, matching charge_counter) and expose charge_now from the
battery charge counter.

Evidence (FP6, kernel 7.2.0-fp6-nixos4, 2026-10-24, read-only):
  charge_counter=4043618 at capacity 91  (design 4415 mAh -> 91.6 %)
  charge_full / charge_full_design: "No data available"
  upower: energy 0 Wh, energy-full 0 Wh

Not built or booted. Build only as part of a normal reviewed kernel trial.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-24 12:48:07.556065702 +0300
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-10-24 12:48:07.584354999 +0300
@@ -438,6 +438,7 @@
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP] = BATT_TEMP,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY] = BATT_TECHNOLOGY,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER] =  BATT_CHG_COUNTER,
+	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW] = BATT_CHG_COUNTER,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT] = BATT_CYCLE_COUNT,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN] =  BATT_CHG_FULL_DESIGN,
 	[POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL] = BATT_CHG_FULL,
@@ -582,7 +583,11 @@
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW:
 		if (unit != QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh)
 			return -ENODATA;
-		val->intval = battmgr->status.capacity;
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350 ||
+		    battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
+			val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_count;
+		else
+			val->intval = battmgr->status.capacity;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER:
 		val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_count;
@@ -875,6 +880,7 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
@@ -907,6 +913,7 @@
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TECHNOLOGY,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_COUNTER,
+	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_NOW,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL,
@@ -1658,6 +1665,16 @@
 	else
 		battmgr->variant = QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350;
 
+	/*
+	 * The SM8350-family property interface reports CHG_FULL, CHG_FULL_DESIGN
+	 * and CHG_COUNTER in uAh. battmgr->unit is otherwise only filled in by
+	 * the SC8280XP-style info response, so it stayed at mWh (0) and every
+	 * listed charge_* property returned -ENODATA (observed on FP6/milos).
+	 */
+	if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350 ||
+	    battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(battmgr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
